    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d929">

                <pb facs="1046" n="902" xml:id="pg902"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">437.11H23/10: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Williamson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-07-16T15:00:00-05:00">July 16, 1926—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:43 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>119. Department’s instruction 720, June 12, 1926. Foreign Office reply in Harrah
                    case received yesterday. Text and translation go forward in tomorrow’s
                        pouch.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d929-f1"/> In 18–page note Government
                    courteously but categorically refuses to entertain proposal of arbitration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williamson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
